From 85f6386eb63dedd567fffc76bfca79790b3862fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mukayi <1515982581@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:36:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] test(metrics): drive the real report_step, not the
 test's own to_thread

`test_slow_backend_does_not_block_concurrent_ingestion` called
`asyncio.to_thread(service._report_to_backends, ...)` itself, so it asserted that
the test's own `to_thread` works. It never drove `report_step`, which is the code
that decides whether the fan-out runs on the event loop: deleting the handler's
`await asyncio.to_thread(...)` and inlining the call left the test green.

Rewrite it to await the real `report_step` coroutine and a real
`/log_metrics_batch`, with two observers running while the report is in flight: a
10 ms ticker and an ingest that becomes ready 50 ms in. On a blocked loop both land
at ~300 ms; with the fan-out on a worker thread the ingest completes at ~50 ms.

Measured against the baseline commit before F1 (9cccfea): 1 tick and a 425.9 ms
slowest `/health`; after the fix: 29-30 ticks and 126.3 ms. Mutating `report_step`
back to an inline call fails it again, so it detects the defect rather than the
tree.

The class is built with `__new__` because `@serve.ingress` gives it an async
`__init__`, and the real one would open wandb / TensorBoard / ClearML.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b7639f24f0cd305316f0daaccee9dd28bae5f1b5)
